# Line endings are pinned in the repository, not left to each checkout's core.autocrlf.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would check every script out with CRLF, and
# bash then fails on the first line with `$'\r': command not found`. So everything text is LF in the
# working tree on every OS. The files cmd.exe itself reads are CRLF, stored that way and never
# converted (-text), so the vendored gradlew.bat stays byte-identical to Gradle's.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat  -text
*.cmd  -text

*.jar  binary
*.nbt  binary
*.png  binary
*.zip  binary
